The compilation errors indicate that the devicetree macros for the `zephyr,adc-emul` device instance are not being generated. This typically happens when the corresponding devicetree node is not enabled (i.e., its `status` property is not `"okay"`).

The test `tests/drivers/adc/adc_emul/src/main.c` uses `DT_INST(0, zephyr_adc_emul)` to refer to the emulated ADC device. The macros `DEVICE_DT_GET` and `DT_PROP` require the devicetree node to be enabled so that the build system generates the necessary C preprocessor definitions and device structures.

The board devicetree files (e.g., for `native_posix`) define the `adc-emul` node with `status = "disabled"` by default. The test's overlay file, `tests/drivers/adc/adc_emul/app.overlay`, modifies this node but fails to enable it.

The fix is to add `status = "okay";` to the `&adc0` node in the overlay file to enable the device for the test.

tests/drivers/adc/adc_emul/app.overlay
<<<<<<<< SEARCH
&adc0 {
	ref-internal-mv = <3300>;
	ref-external1-mv = <5000>;
};
========
&adc0 {
	status = "okay";
	ref-internal-mv = <3300>;
	ref-external1-mv = <5000>;
};
